[  264.4s] NOTE assumption: Documents conflict on identity attempts: the API says three wrong answers end the check, but brief C.2 says the second wrong answer (across both questions) ends verification. The brief governs the agent: max_wrong = 2.
[  264.4s] NOTE assumption: Brief B.1 prescribes 'This call is recorded.' The spec rules allow 'recorded' only in promise lines, so the opening says 'We record this call.' instead, keeping the meaning.
[  264.4s] NOTE assumption: Brief B.1 says to ask for {first_name} {last_name}; no title variable is given, so confirm_ask uses first and last name.
[  264.4s] NOTE assumption: The opening question 'Can you pay the full overdue amount of EUR {amount} today?' is written without 'EUR' because {amount} is already spoken with the currency.
[  264.4s] NOTE assumption: Opening question counts as proposal 1 (F.1): opening_is_attempt = true, ladder step 1 is full amount today, and band attempts are the brief's totals (Tier 1: 2, Tier 2: 3). Tier 1 is therefore the opening plus the full amount on the deadline.
[  264.4s] NOTE assumption: Tier 2 deadline: the 15th of this month, rolled to next month's 15th only if it is before today (the 15th itself is today's deadline), then moved forward to the next business day (roll_before_adjust = true).
[  264.4s] NOTE assumption: deadline_adjust = next_business_day: brief D.3 moves a non-business deadline forward and D.4 offers the next business day for a non-business date. Tier 1 deadlines are always business days.
[  264.4s] NOTE assumption: Ladder step 2 is half the overdue amount (pct:50) rounded up to a whole euro (an already-whole amount stays), then raised to the floor if lower. Steps identical to an earlier proposal (opening included) are skipped and do not count (F.3).
[  264.4s] NOTE assumption: Overdraft floor: 25% of overdue_eur rounded up to the whole euro (an already-whole amount stays); if overdue_eur is below 100, the floor is the whole overdue amount.
[  264.4s] NOTE assumption: Hardship (G.3) has no support transfer: sympathy only, no question, hardship notes on remaining products, close no_promise/hardship. Modelled as hardship_transfer 'direct' with transfer_support queue empty; hardship_short/hardship_declined lines are fallbacks only.
[  264.4s] NOTE assumption: Memo OPS-26-31 is dated: close reason 'hardship' becomes 'financial_difficulty' for calls on or after 2026-11-04 (event_changes). add_note reason 'hardship' is unchanged.
[  264.4s] NOTE assumption: Outcome priority when no promise is recorded and products ended differently: service_error, refused, dispute, paid. A mix of only disputed and paid products is not covered by the table and closes as dispute.
[  264.4s] NOTE assumption: date_rules.next_weekday: the brief is silent; default 'following_week' used.
[  264.4s] NOTE assumption: max_unclear: the brief is silent; default 3 used.
[  264.4s] NOTE assumption: max_not_talk: the brief is silent; default 2 used.
[  264.4s] NOTE assumption: purpose_is_decline: the brief is silent; default true (asking about the call instead of answering is treated as declining, told once why we ask).
[  264.4s] NOTE assumption: Callback business_days_only false: the brief allows 'today or the next business day' without restricting today to business days.
[  264.4s] NOTE assumption: promise_change: the brief is silent; the agent says the promise cannot be changed on this call.
[  264.4s] NOTE assumption: sms_line empty: the brief requires no message after a recorded promise.
